  "text": "끕\n\n compartments của=[\n compartment: Large boxed meals: 8 people // meals per meal = 3 chicken sandwiches + 2 vegetarian sandwiches + 3 salads = 8 meals\n compartments of vegetarian sandwiches:\n compartment: Small boxed meals: 4 people // meals per meal = 2 chicken sandwiches + 1 vegetarian sandwich + 2 salads = 5 meals\n compartments of salads:\n meal: Individual packages // meals per meal = 1 chicken sandwich + 1 vegetarian sandwich + 1 salad = 3 meals\n compartments of chicken sandwiches:\n\n compartment: Each group has 8 people, so we need to calculate how many large boxes and small boxes of individual servings will equate to an integer number of servings across all three groups to maintain consistency in the ratio.\n\n compartment: Since we're trying to make sure that each group gets the same amount of chicken sandwiches, vegetarian sandwiches, and salads, we must ensure the ratio of chicken sandwiches per person is the same across all groups. Since this is still an iterative process:\n\n compartment: Since we're trying to make sure each person gets a consistent amount of chicken sandwiches, vegetarian sandwiches, and salads, we must ensure the ratio of chicken sandwiches per person is the same across all three groups.\n\n compartment: Small boxed meals: 4 people // servings per meal = 2 chicken sandwiches + 1 vegetarian sandwich + 2 salads = 5 servings\n compartment: Large boxed meals: 8 people // servings per meal = 3 chicken sandwiches + 2 vegetarian sandwiches + 3 salads = 8 servings\n compartment: Individual packages: 1 person // servings per meal = 1 chicken sandwich + 1 vegetarian sandwich + 1 salad = 3 servings\n compartment: Large boxed meals: 8 servings per meal * r (ratio of chicken sandwiches per person across all groups, should be a whole number)\n\n compartment: Small boxed meals: 5 servings per meal * r (2 chicken sandwiches + 1 vegetarian sandwich + 2 salads) = 10 servings per meal * s (ratio of vegetarian sandwiches per person across all groups)\n\n compartment: Individual packages:\n\n compartment: 3 servings per meal * r (1 chicken sandwich + 1 vegetarian sandwich + 1 salad) = 6 servings per meal * t (ratio of salads per person across all groups)\n compartment: Large boxed meals, small boxed meals and individual packages have to complement each other to yield integer values for all servings.\n\n compartment: Finding the smallest ratio r, s, and t that solves for an integer number of servings for each person for all three groups.\n\n compartment: To meet the requirements, one strategy is to:\n\n compartment: create the smallest food set, 8 chicken sandwiches + 5 vegetarian sandwiches + 8 salads. The whole ratio of chicken and vegetarian sandwiches and salads per person should be 1 : 1.5 : 1 and then compounded across all three groups of people.\n\n compartment: Since 8 positive numbers must contain only integers in closed expressions, the smallest r is 4 because: 8 * 4 = 32 chicken sandwiches. \n compartment: Or 5 * 4 = 20 vegetarian sandwiches.\n compartment: Or 8 * 4 = 32 salads.\n compartment: Or 3 * 4 * 4 = 48 chicken sandwiches per person, but then each person has chicken sandwiches. \n\n compartment: Choosing 10 vegetarian sandwiches should yield an close enough approximation of 8 and it can do so! So 5 * 3 = 15 vegetarian sandwiches, close enough approximation.\n compartment: Choosing 32 salads should also yield an close enough approximation of 8 and it can do so! So 8 * 3 = 24 salads, close enough approximation.\n compartment: Smaller food set: 4 chicken sandwiches + 3 vegetarian sandwiches + 32 salads\n\n compartment: This yields an integer number of servings for 8 x r = 32 chicken sandwiches.\n compartment: This yields an integer number of servings for 20 x r = 20 vegetarian sandwiches.\n compartment: This yields an integer number of servings for 48 x r = 48 salads.\n compartment: Which, yields an integer number of servings for 3 + 32n = 35 ... 35 is our smallest possible partial total across all three groups.\n\n compartment: Check our total:\n\n compartment: Chicken sandwiches: 32 * 4 = 128\n compartment: Vegetarian sandwiches: 20 * 4 = 80\n compartment: Salads: 48 * 4 = 192\n\n compartment: Making sure all partial totals add back up around an integer: \n compartment: 128 + 80 + 192 = 300. Which is very close.\n compartment: Adding in the final, closes approximation to an integer in our total from above: 8 chicken sandwiches + 8 vegetarian sandwiches + 32 salads, a total of 48 per person = 36 for our whole group.",
